<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wernigerode</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wernigerode is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a> on the northern edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harz">Harz</a>, known for its half-timbered town hall and old town. From 1429 it belonged to the counts of Stolberg, whose Stolberg-Wernigerode line rebuilt its hilltop castle as a historicist palace in the 19th century. It is the starting point of the narrow-gauge railway to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brocken">Brocken</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wernigerode.jpg" alt="Wernigerode" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GZagatta · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schloss_Wernigerode_nach_Sonnenuntergang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
